import{_ as o,o as t,c as a,a2 as s}from"./chunks/framework.BN3Eol-0.js";const u=JSON.parse('{"title":"UXD-029 — Planet heroes: the whole disc on black, planets only","description":"","frontmatter":{},"headers":[],"relativePath":"uxs/decisions/UXD-029-planet-heroes-whole-disc-on-black.md","filePath":"uxs/decisions/UXD-029-planet-heroes-whole-disc-on-black.md"}'),n={name:"uxs/decisions/UXD-029-planet-heroes-whole-disc-on-black.md"};function r(l,e,i,c,d,h){return t(),a("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[s('<h1 id="uxd-029-—-planet-heroes-the-whole-disc-on-black-planets-only" tabindex="-1">UXD-029 — Planet heroes: the whole disc on black, planets only <a class="header-anchor" href="#uxd-029-—-planet-heroes-the-whole-disc-on-black-planets-only" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;UXD-029 — Planet heroes: the whole disc on black, planets only&quot;">​</a></h1><ul><li><strong>Status</strong>: accepted (built: frame, Mars hero, EP3 relocation)</li><li><strong>Date</strong>: 2026-11-13 (proposed and decided)</li><li><strong>Decider</strong>: the operator, 2026-11-13 — recommendations of <code>docs/wip/2026-11-13-slice-C10-brief.md</code> §12 approved as written (&quot;I am OK on 25 recommendations&quot;, commit <code>ec0ceeb9be2</code>, for C6 to C10 together), then the side-by-side sheet: &quot;whole disc for the eight unchanged pictures: yes&quot;; Mars: first the 2018 picture (slot 04) with a tighter crop, then, after seeing it, <strong>the SVS true-colour globe</strong> (decision 4).</li><li><strong>Answers</strong>: EP2, EP3 of the UX feedback plan; slice C10; BACKFILL B-033</li><li><strong>Builds on</strong>: <a href="./UXD-018-panel-shell-and-actions">UXD-018</a> (the panel&#39;s hero: 16:9 box, no hover glow), <a href="./UXD-023-star-and-outer-panels-follow-the-planet-pattern">UXD-023</a> (the star and outer panels keep the 16:9 cover)</li><li><strong>Changes</strong>: <code>src/lib/components/PlanetPanel.svelte</code> and <code>SmallBodyPanel.svelte</code> (Pluto only; <code>heroClass=&quot;planet-hero&quot;</code>), <code>src/lib/styles/panel-tabs.css</code> (<code>.planet-hero</code>), <code>src/lib/data/planet-heroes.test.ts</code> (new), <code>tests/e2e/planet-heroes.spec.ts</code> (new); <a href="./../UXS-001">UXS-001</a>, <code>docs/concept/05_Design_System.md</code> 5.3, the change inventory, BACKFILL, <code>AGENTS.md</code>, <code>scripts/IMAGE-PIPELINE.md</code>, the component README</li></ul><h2 id="context" tabindex="-1">Context <a class="header-anchor" href="#context" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Context&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The panel hero is a 16:9 cover crop (400 x 225 px). A square picture of a disc that fills its frame loses 44 % of its height, so the poles of Mercury, Venus, Earth, Uranus, Neptune and Pluto were cut. By measurement of the served pictures the disc spans 77 to 94 % of the picture height for those planets (Jupiter 77 %, Saturn&#39;s rings 52 %). &quot;Whole-disc heroes&quot; cannot be had by picking pictures; it needs a frame.</p><p>Pluto is drawn by <code>SmallBodyPanel</code>, and its hero is <code>small-bodies/pluto/01</code> (New Horizons, enhanced colour, a full disc), <strong>not</strong> <code>planets/pluto/01</code> that the C10 brief listed: the planets gallery for Pluto is not what the panel shows.</p><h2 id="decision" tabindex="-1">Decision <a class="header-anchor" href="#decision" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Decision&quot;">​</a></h2><ol><li><p><strong>The rule.</strong> A planet panel&#39;s hero is one picture of the planet itself, in natural or published colour: no artist concept, no spacecraft in frame, no map, inset or diagram. The nine heroes at this commit meet it (checked by title in <code>planet-heroes.test.ts</code>, and by eye on the sheet); Earth 04 (Apollo-Soyuz) and Venus 03 (Magellan concept) are in the Gallery tab, not the hero slot.</p></li><li><p><strong>The frame.</strong> Planet panels draw the hero with <code>object-fit: contain</code> in the same 16:9 box, on pure black (<code>.planet-hero</code> in <code>panel-tabs.css</code>). The pictures&#39; own space is <code>rgb(0,0,0)</code> (measured at the outer two pixels of every hero: 0,0,0; Jupiter 2,2,2, Neptune 1,1,0): the earlier translucent button ground over the panel colour (about 2,2,7) showed as a faint rectangle, so the ground is <code>#000</code>. Only planets: star, outer and black-hole panels keep the 16:9 cover (UXD-023).</p></li><li><p><strong>The cards and the entity page are unchanged.</strong> The collectible card&#39;s hero band is a cover crop under a fade (it shares the file, not the frame); <code>/explore/&lt;id&gt;</code> draws no hero picture.</p></li><li><p><strong>Mars (built).</strong> The hero is the new slot <code>planets/mars/06</code>: NASA Goddard SVS &quot;Mars Rotate (True Color)&quot; (<a href="https://svs.gsfc.nasa.gov/659/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">SVS 659</a>, Commons file of the same name, PD-NASA), a <strong>globe rendered in true colour from Mars Global Surveyor MOLA and Viking data, not a single photograph</strong>, 2560 x 1920 with the disc 1635 px across (85 % of the height, like Earth 04 and Jupiter 01). Slots 03 and 04 stay in the gallery. The provenance title and the 14-locale alt text say it is a rendering. Not taken: the 2018 Hubble slot 04 as is (the disc is 51 % of its picture), cropped (a 970 px square: the operator judged it too soft next to Earth and Jupiter), and a 2016 Hubble photograph (candidate A of the sheet, disc 69 %). The operator chose the SVS globe on 2026-11-13; Earth 04 is likewise a rendered composite.</p></li><li><p><strong>EP3 relocation (built, decision 3a).</strong> Earth 04 (Apollo-Soyuz, a spacecraft in frame) moved to <code>missions/apollo-soyuz/05</code> and Venus 03 (Magellan artist concept) to <code>missions/magellan/06</code>, with <code>move-image-to-gallery.ts</code>; the gap each left was closed with <code>drop-gallery-slots.mjs --gone</code> (new flag: the slots are already gone, only renumber). Earth&#39;s hero override followed (<code>05.jpg</code> to <code>04.jpg</code>: same picture). Planet galleries: Earth 4, Venus 4, Mars 6.</p></li></ol><h2 id="consequences" tabindex="-1">Consequences <a class="header-anchor" href="#consequences" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Consequences&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li>All nine discs show whole at 400 px and at phone width; discs are 77 to 94 % of the box height (Saturn smaller: its rings fill the width).</li><li>A hero&#39;s <code>position</code> (override file) has no effect on a contain frame.</li><li>Not taken: a taller 1:1 hero (175 px more height above the tabs against UXD-018); keeping the cover and accepting the crop.</li></ul><h2 id="not-done" tabindex="-1">Not done <a class="header-anchor" href="#not-done" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Not done&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li>The collectible card&#39;s hero band is a cover crop, so Mars&#39;s card shows a band of the globe, not the whole disc (as for every planet).</li><li>EP3 borderline slots (Venus 02 Maat Mons, Earth 01 &quot;Earthrise&quot; visualisation) stay, as recommended; no other slot was audited by eye.</li><li>Whether every explicit override entry should carry <code>disc: true</code> (brief decision 5a): not built; the data test guards the hero slot instead.</li></ul><h2 id="verification" tabindex="-1">Verification <a class="header-anchor" href="#verification" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Verification&quot;">​</a></h2><p><code>src/lib/data/planet-heroes.test.ts</code> (every override inside its gallery, every hero slot on disk, no artwork or spacecraft word in a hero title) and <code>tests/e2e/planet-heroes.spec.ts</code> (nine panels: <code>object-fit: contain</code>, black ground, 16:9 box). Run counts are in the C10 row of the change inventory.</p>',13)])])}const g=o(n,[["render",r]]);export{u as __pageData,g as default};
